== NUMERIC_FAST (the shipped build) ==
  -- core/gemm_identity_check.mojo
== core/gemm_identity_check.mojo [FAST] ==
check_gram_chunk_count_is_pinned OK [FAST]: k partitions into 240 chunks, and the workspace-sizing predicate independently implies the same 240 (pinned constant is 128; under FAST this number is the machine's own and under IDENTICAL it is the constant)
check_gram_arm_is_pinned OK [FAST]: nvidia/amd rows answer False and bit-identical answers True; this build's arm compiles against column apple, which takes the split-K kernel at 32x32x4M: True and at 128-square: True. A False there is not a bug -- it is the FAST dispatch handing the Gram shape to linalg.matmul, and it is exactly what DEVIATION 521 stops an IDENTICAL build from doing.
check_gemm_tn_refuses_over_capacity OK [FAST]: 256x256x512 still runs on the transpose+matmul arm
check_pinned_gemm_is_batch_invariant REPORT [FAST]: 256 overlapping cells on the vendor matmul, n=4 as the reference -- n=64 differs in 0 cells, n=256 differs in 0. A nonzero count here is not a bug, it is the measurement that prices the pin: it means the shipped arm's answer for a row depends on how many other rows were in the launch.
check_pinned_gemv_matches_oracle OK [FAST]: 37 elements over k=91 within 7.438901403755693e-07 of an ascending Float64 fold, no poison survived
  -- core/column_stats_identity_check.mojo
check_column_stats_row_is_pinned OK (FAST): K_LIB_COLUMN_STATS is classified as a float fold; per-column widths apple 128 nvidia 128 amd 128 (identical column 128 ). STATS_TPB 128
check_column_stats_fold_shape OK (FAST): the library fold ran (column 0 mean 29594.826/0x0x46e735a7 | xty 110270235000.0/0x0x51cd64f2 ); host halving mean 29594.824/0x0x46e735a6 vs sequential 29594.82/0x0x46e735a4 | host halving xty 110270230000.0/0x0x51cd64f1 vs sequential 110270240000.0/0x0x51cd64f3 . The device differs from the host halving tree in 2 of 8 mean columns and 2 of 8 xty columns, and halving vs sequential differ in every column -- so the IDENTICAL arm's equality has teeth. Those two counts ARE the local strength of the reach proof: they are how many columns of this fixture would catch a `block.sum` left in an IDENTICAL build on THIS backend. The defect they stand in for -- AMD's 64-wide wavefront -- is not observable here at all; only E1 sees that one.
check_xty_contraction_pin OK (FAST): this backend contracts both spellings (0 of 32 columns separate the arms), and the shipped kernel matches both. The contraction pin is bit-inert on this column; the FAST bits are untouched by DEVIATION 523.
  -- checks/gram_splitk_check.mojo
check_gram_splitk_oracle OK: split-K arm matches the Float64 oracle per cell and is bitwise symmetric at 10 shapes (m 1..128 covering all three CELLS widths and both staging-copy arms; k odd, prime, below/above the 240-chunk grid, and never a chunk multiple)
check_gram_vendor_arm OK: transpose+matmul arm matches the Float64 oracle per cell at 33x33x257 within mag x 1.3822140584440566e-05 (vendor matmul, fp32 on column apple; the fp32 budget plus the closed product's serial-fold allowance); bitwise symmetry asserted
check_gram_tf32_bound_separates OK: operands rounded to 10 mantissa bits (8479 of 8481 moved) through the fp32 split-K kernel at 33x33x257 land worst mag-relative 6.793221760929424e-05 at cell (11, 17) from the exact oracle: REJECTED by the fp32 budget 1.3822140584440566e-05, ADMITTED by the TF32 bound 0.0010138221405844405 -- the two per-column tolerances of DEVIATION 540 separate a TF32-class product from an fp32 one on this box (the H100 leg measured 2.4e-5 on the real vendor arm at this shape)
check_gram_dispatch OK: predicate routes 32x32x4M/1x1x7/128x128 to split-K and 129x129/768x768/m!=n to the fallback; staging copy vectorizes m=32/4/128 and falls back scalar at m=33/1; register tile owns m=32/64/128 (2x2/4x4/8x8) and declines m=1/3/33 to the strided arm; wrapper verified per cell on arm 'split-K' at 32x32x100003 (fp32 (pinned or split-K kernel)) and arm 'transpose+matmul (FAST) / REFUSED (IDENTICAL)' at 768x768x257 (vendor matmul, fp32 on column apple)
check_gram_centered_fused OK: fused centered read is bitwise equal to center-then-split-K at every cell (m=4/32/33, k=8192/100003/257, both workspace paths), and x is bit-identical afterwards
  -- decomposition/checks/jacobi_check.mojo
check_jacobi_fold_width_is_pinned OK (FAST): K_LIB_JACOBI_EIGH resolves to 32/32/64 (Apple/NVIDIA/AMD) against the identity floor's 32; this build compiles against 32, a power of two. NOTE: 32 threads is HALF an AMD CDNA wavefront -- under IDENTICAL the halving tree touches only the 32 slots real threads wrote, so that is a scheduling question there and not a numeric one.
check_jacobi_fold_shape OK (FAST): the library fold ran and pinned_block_sum is it, bit for bit ( 16777262.0 == 16777262.0 ). Host halving 16777262.0 and sequential 16777278.0 differ, so the IDENTICAL arm's equality has teeth.
check_jacobi_device_sizes OK: 16, 32, 33, 64, 128, 256 all satisfy A V = V diag(lambda) and V^T V = I. The 32-feature cap is gone.
